Apple's press release for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-homepod-mini-2/">HomePod mini 2</a> last month touted "rich sound" and "advanced computational audio," but it did not explicitly mention if the second-generation model has better sound compared to the original. A few early reviews of the speaker, however, said that audio quality has in fact improved.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Four-HomePod-Mini-2-Surround-Sound.jpg" alt="" width="1530" height="861" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075617" /><br/>
Apple's tech specs pages for both the HomePod mini 2 and the original HomePod mini mention a "full-range driver" and "dual passive radiators for deep bass and crisp high frequencies," so the core speaker hardware is seemingly unchanged. However, the HomePod mini 2 is equipped with a much newer S10 chip that could use advanced algorithms to optimize sound in an improved manner compared to the S5 chip in the original model.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.cnet.com/home/smart-home/apple-homepod-mini-2-tiny-powerful-upgrades/"><em>CNET</em>'s Tyler Lacoma said</a> the HomePod mini 2 has "much better sound" than the original model.<br/>
<br/>
From his article:<blockquote>Playing the same audio at the same volume on each speaker, I repeatedly switched between them while streaming Apple Lossless audio via Apple Music. The results were always the same: The new Mini 2 had significantly greater range and louder, clearer audio than the first HomePod Mini. It wasn't just noticeable: It was a big enough difference to completely change my mind about a speaker that didn't seem worth it on paper. If you want sound that can actually fill a room without losing quality, the HomePod Mini 2 is by far the preferable pick.</blockquote><a href="https://www.cultofmac.com/reviews/homepod-mini-2-review-apple-smart-speaker"><em>Cult of Mac</em>'s Ed Hardy said</a> likewise:<blockquote>To my ears, the second-gen version sounds noticeably better. Especially the stronger bass. I did a side-by-side comparison with HomePod mini 2 and my original model, and the new model definitely came out ahead.</blockquote>Another benefit of the S10 chip that Apple did not emphasize: Siri is apparently much faster for basic requests such as playing a song and smart home commands, according to <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1024108/homepod-mini-2-hands-on-siri-smart-home-mac-speaker"><em>The Verge</em>'s Jennifer Pattison Tuohy</a>. However, this is based on what Apple now calls Siri Classic, as the more intelligent and personalized Siri AI will not be available on the HomePod mini 2 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/homepod-mini-2-siri-ai-coming-later/">until a future software update</a>, according to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
